  "method": "Published customer payload with only the reviewed claim resilience, scope amendment and generic program-boundary overlay. No private source rebuild. 5.9 adds the reviewed expired-claim narrowing fix to src/claim-scope.js (byte-identical to its source input) with ported tests. 5.10 ports reviewed check-in capabilities from source 3.9.1 by adaptation, not byte copy: path-traversal guard, 16 MiB status buffer, pinned base commit, scope-change holds in finish and release, a user-started claim sweep, and scoped sparse checkouts with explicit intent for large full checkouts. Disk-capacity admission and every machine-specific dependency are excluded. 5.10.1 ports source fix 86e05a0de: finish and release audit sparse scope from the merge base with the claim's target branch, falling back to the pinned base, so files merged in from the target are not flagged.",
